<h2>Buying tickets</h2>
<p>Tickets are sold by the box office named on each event page, which may be a partner organisation or a ticketing platform. That seller’s terms of sale apply to your purchase. Nothing in these terms limits your rights under the Australian Consumer Law.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Cancelled events.</strong> If an event is cancelled, you are entitled to a refund of the ticket price through the seller.</li>
<li><strong>Changes.</strong> Line-ups, set times and venues can change. If an event is rescheduled, your ticket is valid for the new date, or you can ask the seller about a refund.</li>
<li><strong>Resale.</strong> Please only buy from the seller on our event page. Tickets bought from unofficial resellers may not be valid.</li>
</ul>
<h2>At the event</h2>
<ul>
<li>Our events are usually held at licensed venues. Age limits are shown on the event page; bring photo ID.</li>
<li>Venue conditions of entry apply, including bag checks. Entry can be refused, or you can be asked to leave, for unsafe or disrespectful behaviour, without a refund.</li>
<li>Our nights are photographed and filmed for promotion. Tell our crew if you prefer not to be photographed.</li>
</ul>
